Neon containers port (M6): clearing browsing data also clears the containers.

A removal that names no storage partition (the "Delete browsing data" dialog
for all spaces, clear on exit, an extension's browsingData call) clears the
data types that live on a storage partition in every used container too, with
the same time range and origin filter. Ported from brave-core v1.100.58
(bd6d26d1): BraveBrowsingDataRemoverDelegate::RemoveEmbedderData
(browser/browsing_data/brave_browsing_data_remover_delegate.cc) becomes a hunk
in ChromeBrowsingDataRemoverDelegate::RemoveEmbedderData, and
browser/containers/used_container_storage_partitions.{h,cc} is copied as is.

The per-container removals are queued behind the removal that started them.
Neon adds one thing Brave lacks: the clear-on-exit observer waits for them
(an empty removal queued after them), or the browser exits before they run.

